          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                \-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,1)
                \-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            in the usual sense of the word. The prefix
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categorical
            types of topoi in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theory
            such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topoi"} topos
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%280%2C1%29-topos"} (0,1)-topos
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
          %p
            Similarly, a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                Grothendieck
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                Grothendieck
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+%280%2C1%29-topos"} Grothendieck (0,1)-topos
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            (or
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
          %p
            Note that a 1-topos is not exactly a particular sort of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
            or
            = succeed "-topos," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            is not a particular sort of 1-topos. The (1,2)-category of locales (i.e. (0,1)-topoi) embeds fully in the 2-category of Grothendieck 1-topoi by taking sheaves, but a locale is not identical to its topos of sheaves (and in fact no nontrivial 1-topos can be a poset), in that the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            can
            %em not
            be filled by a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
